From: Cloud Claude <cloud@spikeyolo>
Date: 2026-05-31
Subject: [DEBUG BRING-UP ONLY] skip FSBL DDRInitCheck self-test

UNSAFE FOR PRODUCTION — bring-up patch.

The Zynq-7000 FSBL runs a pattern-readback DDR self-test (DDRInitCheck())
right after ps7_init. On our ZYBO Z7-20 the test fails on byte lane 3
(reads 0xFF for mixed patterns, uniform OK), tripping FsblHookFallback() at
PC=0x578 with REBOOT_STATUS=0x400000 — before ever reaching u-boot, so no
UART/JTAG access to a TRAINED DDR controller.

All prior JTAG DDR readbacks were taken through this FAILED-init halted
controller (training never completed). To get the first uncontaminated,
fully-trained DDR state, we need to skip this in-FSBL test, boot to Linux,
then run the decisive bench tests (POST-TRAIN slave regs + 0x55-vs-0xAA
symmetry + memtest) from a quiescent controller.

This patch is for *bring-up debug only*. Production FSBL must include the
DDR self-test. After root cause is confirmed and fixed, remove the
SRC_URI entry in fsbl-firmware_%.bbappend.

Reference: Main Claude 2026-05-31 reframe + Cloud Claude
ddr_debug_reports.md Option B.

--- a/lib/sw_apps/zynq_fsbl/src/main.c
+++ b/lib/sw_apps/zynq_fsbl/src/main.c
@@ -287,21 +287,18 @@

 #if defined(XPAR_PS7_DDR_0_S_AXI_BASEADDR) || defined(XPAR_PS7_DDR_0_BASEADDRESS)

-    /*
-     * DDR Read/write test
-     */
-	Status = DDRInitCheck();
-	if (Status == XST_FAILURE) {
-		fsbl_printf(DEBUG_GENERAL,"DDR_INIT_FAIL \r\n");
-		/* Error Handling here */
-		OutputStatus(DDR_INIT_FAIL);
-		/*
-		 * Calling FsblHookFallback instead of Fallback
-		 * since, devcfg driver is not yet initialized
-		 */
-		FsblHookFallback();
-	}
+	/* CLOUD-DEBUG-PATCH: DDR self-test skipped per Main 80e7b1d reframe +
+	 * cloud ddr_debug_reports.md Option B. Lane-3 mixed-pattern collapse
+	 * trips this in pre-train controller; skip to reach a TRAINED DDR
+	 * state, then bench-test from Linux. UNSAFE FOR PRODUCTION. */
+	fsbl_printf(DEBUG_GENERAL,"\r\n*** DEBUG BUILD: FSBL DDRInitCheck SKIPPED ***\r\n");
+	fsbl_printf(DEBUG_GENERAL,"*** Bring-up image: bench-test DDR from Linux ***\r\n\r\n");
+	(void)Status;


 #endif
